## Custom emoji and symbols

In Writeout (Insert > Custom Emoji) and Bitbook (Skills > Custom Emoji / Symbol) you can draw your own emoji or symbol on a square canvas with a pen, a gel pen, a marker, a neon tube or a dashed line, and it goes into your text like a picture the size of a letter. Double-click it later to keep drawing. Saved as text it is `@@emoji="d='g:ff7a1a:6:10,20;30,40',size='md'"`: each stroke is `ink:color:width:x,y;x,y;...` on a 100 by 100 square, strokes are joined with `|`, and the size is `sm`, `md` or `lg`.

## Dark Gel chips

Sixteen midnight neon pills sharing one dark design, built into Keydown (they used to be a Marketplace pack, so nothing needs installing)! Write `~CPR~text~CPR~` with a color letter after CP (R O A Y L G E T C S B I V F P, and Q for slate)!

* `~CPR~text~CPR~` Chip Red: ~CPR~Chip Red~CPR~
* `~CPO~text~CPO~` Chip Orange: ~CPO~Chip Orange~CPO~
* `~CPA~text~CPA~` Chip Amber: ~CPA~Chip Amber~CPA~
* `~CPY~text~CPY~` Chip Yellow: ~CPY~Chip Yellow~CPY~
* `~CPL~text~CPL~` Chip Lime: ~CPL~Chip Lime~CPL~
* `~CPG~text~CPG~` Chip Green: ~CPG~Chip Green~CPG~
* `~CPE~text~CPE~` Chip Emerald: ~CPE~Chip Emerald~CPE~
* `~CPT~text~CPT~` Chip Teal: ~CPT~Chip Teal~CPT~
* `~CPC~text~CPC~` Chip Cyan: ~CPC~Chip Cyan~CPC~
* `~CPS~text~CPS~` Chip Sky: ~CPS~Chip Sky~CPS~
* `~CPB~text~CPB~` Chip Blue: ~CPB~Chip Blue~CPB~
* `~CPI~text~CPI~` Chip Indigo: ~CPI~Chip Indigo~CPI~
* `~CPV~text~CPV~` Chip Violet: ~CPV~Chip Violet~CPV~
* `~CPF~text~CPF~` Chip Fuchsia: ~CPF~Chip Fuchsia~CPF~
* `~CPP~text~CPP~` Chip Pink: ~CPP~Chip Pink~CPP~
* `~CPQ~text~CPQ~` Chip Slate: ~CPQ~Chip Slate~CPQ~

## Bullet styles

Start a line with a mark and a space to make a bullet, and the mark picks the look. Lines with the same mark stay one list, and a new mark starts a new list!

* `* item` is the round bullet
- `- item` is a dash
+ `+ item` is a green plus
. `. item` is a ring
~ `~ item` is an orange diamond
= `= item` is a purple arrow

## Spoilers

Write `*sp(text)` to hide words behind a dark bar until someone clicks them, like *sp(the butler did it)! Click again to hide them. Saved as text it stays `*sp(text)`. The words cannot contain a `)`.

## Blockquote looks

A line that starts with a symbol, `>` and a space is a quote with a different look, like the plain `> quote` but dressed up. They are all the same kind of quote, only the look changes. Type the line and press Enter (or use Re-format); saving as text gives the same line back. There are 14 looks:

`!> your text` Orange: an orange tinted panel with an orange bar on the left, like the green and red looks.

!> This is how a quote looks in the orange look.

`?> your text` Cyan: a cyan tinted panel with a cyan bar on the left, like the green and red looks.

?> This is how a quote looks in the cyan look.

`>> your text` Pull quote: big centered italic words between two rules, with large quote marks.

>> This is how a quote looks in the pull quote look.

`%> your text` Gradient: a blue to cyan gradient panel with white bold words.

%> This is how a quote looks in the gradient look.

`*> your text` Highlighter: a yellow marker band behind the words.

*> This is how a quote looks in the highlighter look.

`+> your text` Green: a green tinted panel with a green bar on the left.

+> This is how a quote looks in the green look.

`-> your text` Red: a red tinted panel with a red bar on the left.

-> This is how a quote looks in the red look.

`=> your text` Dashed frame: a soft grey box with a dashed border.

=> This is how a quote looks in the dashed frame look.

`~> your text` Whisper: small faded italic words behind a dotted bar.

~> This is how a quote looks in the whisper look.

`$> your text` Paper note: a sticky paper note with a piece of tape on top.

$> This is how a quote looks in the paper note look.

`#> your text` Terminal: a dark terminal panel with monospace words.

#> This is how a quote looks in the terminal look.

`^> your text` Ribbon: a white card with an orange bar and a little ribbon hanging from the top.

^> This is how a quote looks in the ribbon look.

`@> your text` Speech bubble: a blue speech bubble with a tail.

@> This is how a quote looks in the speech bubble look.

`&> your text` Shadow card: a white card that floats above the page on a soft shadow.

&> This is how a quote looks in the shadow card look.

## Rim chips

A glass pill with a thick colored rim: the inside melts from the color at the top to almost clear at the bottom, with a small white shine near the top and words in a deep shade of the color. It is sized by its text (a rim of 0.133em, 0.4em of room at each side). Written `!!#color#text#`, in the same 16 colors as the Aero chips:

* `!!#R#text#` !!#R#red#
* `!!#O#text#` !!#O#orange#
* `!!#GL#text#` !!#GL#gold#
* `!!#Y#text#` !!#Y#yellow#
* `!!#L#text#` !!#L#lime#
* `!!#G#text#` !!#G#green#
* `!!#TU#text#` !!#TU#turquoise#
* `!!#T#text#` !!#T#teal#
* `!!#C#text#` !!#C#cyan#
* `!!#B#text#` !!#B#blue#
* `!!#PR#text#` !!#PR#purple#
* `!!#PK#text#` !!#PK#pink#
* `!!#SL#text#` !!#SL#slate#
* `!!#W#text#` !!#W#white#
* `!!#FG#text#` !!#FG#fog#
* `!!#BK#text#` !!#BK#black#

## Rim liquid chips

A cousin of the Rim Chip with the same size, rim and shine, but filled like a glass of liquid: the color pools at the bottom and clears toward the top (the Rim Chip does the opposite). Written `!!^color#text#`, in the same 16 colors:

* `!!^R#text#` !!^R#red#
